// 소스를 연 채로 인용을 적는다. 요약이 아니라 원문과 그 위치다.
{"id":"e1","source":"w1","locator":"§Input and output tokens","quote":"Per token, decode keeps the GPU busy for a lot longer, which is why output is priced at roughly 5x input.","why":"출력 5배 배수의 근거이자 'roughly' 라는 한정의 근거"}
{"id":"e2","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt caching","quote":"Reading from the cache costs 0.1x the input price, because the server loads the state instead of computing it. Writing tokens into the cache costs a bit more than normal input, up to 2x","why":"캐시 읽기 0.1배와 쓰기 최대 2배"}
{"id":"e3","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt caching (Time)","quote":"the cache expires after an hour on a subscription or five minutes on an API key (ENABLE_PROMPT_CACHING_1H=1 makes it an hour)","why":"캐시 수명과 환경변수"}
{"id":"e4","source":"w1","locator":"§What ends up in the context","quote":"after 30,000 characters Claude Code writes the output to a file and only puts a short preview and the path in the conversation (BASH_MAX_OUTPUT_LENGTH if you want to change it)","why":"30,000자 임계값과 원문이 환경변수로 넘긴 한 줄"}
{"id":"e5","source":"w1","locator":"§What ends up in the context","quote":"A test runner that prints 400 passing tests one line at a time comes in under the limit, and those 400 lines are now part of every remaining turn.","why":"400줄 예시가 임계값 아래라는 서술"}
{"id":"e6","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt caching (순서)","quote":"requests always go out in the same order: tool definitions, then the system prompt, then the conversation (with CLAUDE.md at the front of it)","why":"요청 조립 순서"}
{"id":"e7","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt caching (/model)","quote":"every model has its own cache, so on the next turn the entire conversation gets prefilled again at full price. (This includes opusplan, which switches models every time you go in or out of plan mode.)","why":"모델 전환과 opusplan"}
{"id":"e8","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt caching (Fast mode)","quote":"also part of the key, and the re-prefill happens at fast mode prices, so if you're going to turn it on, turn it on at the start. (Turning it off again is free, cache-wise.)","why":"fast mode 는 끄는 것이 캐시상 무료"}
{"id":"e9","source":"w1","locator":"§Subagents","quote":"A subagent gets its own context window, with its own system prompt, the tools, and your CLAUDE.md, but not your conversation.","why":"서브에이전트가 받는 것과 받지 못하는 것"}
{"id":"e10","source":"w1","locator":"§Model (도해 캡션)","quote":"Curves are for illustration purposes only. They do not represent real benchmark data.","why":"원문 스스로 성능 곡선이 근거가 아니라고 적은 자리"}
{"id":"e11","source":"w1","locator":"§Input and output tokens","quote":"if you already know a session is going to be grunt work, MAX_THINKING_TOKENS=0 claude turns thinking off for that one session (except on Fable 5)","why":"thinking 끄기와 Fable 5 예외"}
{"id":"e12","source":"w1","locator":"§How many turns it stays there","quote":"if you're on a 1M model and would rather have the auto-compact safety net where it used to be, /autocompact 200k puts it back (needs Claude Code v2.1.221+)","why":"autocompact 200k 와 버전 요구"}
{"id":"e13","source":"w1","locator":"§What decides how many tokens a session sends","quote":"Everything that ends up in the conversation, a file Claude read or the output of a command it ran, gets sent again on every turn after it, for the rest of the session.","why":"재전송 구조. 개수 축의 핵심 문장"}
{"id":"e14","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt caching (/rewind tip)","quote":"Rewinding only cuts those turns off the end, so everything before them is still cached and it costs nothing. Compacting rewrites the whole conversation, so it always costs something.","why":"rewind 는 무료, compact 는 항상 비용"}
{"id":"e15","source":"w1","locator":"§Maximizing value","quote":"Being efficient with tokens doesn't mean using fewer of them overall. It means making sure the ones you do use go towards the thing you actually asked for.","why":"문서 3장의 프레이밍 인용"}
{"id":"e16","source":"w1","locator":"§Prompt caching","quote":"This applies on a subscription too. You don't see these prices directly, but the same requests are what draw down your limits.","why":"구독에서도 동일하게 적용"}
{"id":"e17","source":"w1","locator":"§What ends up in the context","quote":"Fix the failing test in utils.test.ts\" skips the searching and costs one Read call for the file, and \"Fix the failing test in @utils.test.ts\" doesn't cost the Read call either","why":"구체성이 턴을 줄인다는 서술"}
{"id":"e18","source":"w1","locator":"§What ends up in the context (@-mention tip)","quote":"The file itself takes up the same room in the context either way, so you only need to mention it once per conversation: it stays there, and @-mentioning it again on a later turn generally attaches a second copy.","why":"두 번 멘션하면 사본이 붙는다"}
{"id":"e19","source":"w2","locator":"issue body","quote":"Output too large (50.2KB). Full output saved to: /home/user/.claude/projects/.../tool-results/toolu_xxx.txt","why":"v2.1.2 이후 디스크 저장 동작이 BASH_MAX_OUTPUT_LENGTH 를 무시한다는 회귀 보고"}
{"id":"e20","source":"w1","locator":"§Subagents","quote":"It pays off when a job produces a lot of output you don't need to keep, like going through a log.","why":"서브에이전트 손익 서술의 범위"}
